── SYNTAX ERROR ──────────────── E0100_javascript_triple_equals.lt:1:39  [E0100]

Stilt compares with `==`, which never converts its operands:

  1 │ fn same(a: i64, b: i64) -> bool { a === b }
    │                                       ^

Two values compare only when they have the same type, so one `==` says it all.

To fix it, write `==`:

  1 │ fn same(a: i64, b: i64) -> bool { a === b }
    │                                       -
